{% comment %}
  pp-fonts — self-hosted custom font override.

  ⚠️ PROVISIONAL / DEV ONLY. These font files (Neue Regrade Extrabold,
  Interstate Bold Condensed) came from font-aggregator sites with
  unverified web-embedding rights — see chat / docs/REQUIREMENTS.md.
  Do NOT launch the site with these files. Swap the two .woff2 files in
  /assets and this snippet is the only place that needs updating.

  Shopify's native font_picker (theme-styles-variables.liquid) can only
  select fonts from Shopify's own library, so it can't reference these
  at all. This overrides the resulting --font-heading / --font-accent
  CSS custom properties instead, after they're set, so every place
  Horizon already uses those roles picks up the custom fonts for free.

  Role assignment (adjust if wrong):
  - heading → Interstate Bold Condensed (big display text, e.g. hero
    headlines)
  - accent  → Neue Regrade Extrabold (nav, buttons, badges — short
    punchy UI text)
{% endcomment %}
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'PP Interstate';
    src: url('{{ 'pp-font-interstate-bold-condensed.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'PP Neue Regrade';
    src: url('{{ 'pp-font-neue-regrade-extrabold.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 800;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  :root {
    --font-heading--family: 'PP Interstate', Impact, 'Arial Narrow', sans-serif;
    --font-heading--style: normal;
    --font-heading--weight: 700;

    --font-accent--family: 'PP Neue Regrade', 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    --font-accent--style: normal;
    --font-accent--weight: 800;
  }

  /* pp: Neue Regrade Extrabold is a heavy display weight; at small UI
     sizes (nav, badges) its counters close up without smoothing help.
     See docs/REQUIREMENTS.md pre-launch blockers for the real fix
     (either a properly-hinted licensed file, or stepping down to a
     lighter weight at small sizes). */
  header-menu {
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
    text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
  }
</style>
